## Conformance examples

- **Do:** `tests/conformance-fixtures/gmn-envelope-complete.ttl`
  - A gmeow:GmnEnvelope carrying all nine contract fields — the three dialect coordinates, the boundary ring, gmeow:accordingTo, gmeow:wasGeneratedBy, gmeow:contentDigest, gmeow:gmnCodebookDigest, and a logic:Correspondence losslessness judgment — satisfies lang:GmnEnvelopeContractShape and validates with no findings\.
- **Do:** `tests/conformance-fixtures/gmn-export-ring-bound.ttl`
  - A gmeow:GmnEnvelope generated by an activity typed gmeow:mentalProcessType gmeow:processExport \(mentation\) and carrying a gmeow:gmnSecurityRing satisfies lang:GmnExportRingBindingShape \(and the pre\-existing lang:GmnEnvelopeContractShape, since every other contract field is also present\) and validates with no findings\.
- **Don't:** `tests/counter-examples/gmn-envelope-dictionary-version-plural.ttl`
  - **Violation code:** `shacl.MaxCountConstraintComponent`
  - The gmeow:GmnEnvelope declares TWO gmeow:gmnDictionaryVersion literals at once \(sh:maxCount 1 on lang:GmnEnvelopeContractShape\) — an alias is meaningless without the ONE pinned dictionary version that minted it, so validation MUST emit shacl\.MaxCountConstraintComponent from gmeow:GmnEnvelope\-shape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI \(lang:GmnMissingEnvelopeField\); the other eight contract fields are present and well\-formed \(R5, version\-pinning is non\-interchangeable\)\. The cell does NOT declare gmeow:expectedSoleFinding, because the report is not sole: it also carries MaxCountConstraintComponent at lang:GmnEnvelopeContractShape\. See the header note on why this slice's reports are wider than one shape\.
- **Don't:** `tests/counter-examples/gmn-envelope-missing-field.ttl`
  - **Violation code:** `shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent`
  - The gmeow:GmnEnvelope omits exactly one of its nine contract fields — the gmeow:gmnSecurityRing boundary ring \(sh:minCount 1 on lang:GmnEnvelopeContractShape\) — so validation MUST emit shacl\.MinCountConstraintComponent from lang:GmnEnvelopeContractShape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI \(lang:GmnMissingEnvelopeField\); the other eight fields are present\. The cell does NOT declare gmeow:expectedSoleFinding, because the report is not sole: it also carries QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent at gmeow:GmnEnvelope\-shape\. See the header note on why this slice's reports are wider than one shape\.
- **Don't:** `tests/counter-examples/gmn-export-crossing-no-ring.ttl`
  - **Violation code:** `shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent`
  - The gmeow:GmnEnvelope is generated by an activity typed gmeow:mentalProcessType gmeow:processExport \(mentation\) but declares no gmeow:gmnSecurityRing \(the sh:sparql of lang:GmnExportRingBindingShape\), so validation MUST emit shacl\.SPARQLConstraintComponent \(lang:GmnUnringedExportCrossing\)\. The pre\-existing sh:minCount 1 of lang:GmnEnvelopeContractShape ALSO fires on the same missing field \(shacl\.MinCountConstraintComponent, lang:GmnMissingEnvelopeField\) — an honest double finding, since ring\-absence is inherently covered by both the general envelope\-contract gate and this export\-specific binding gate; gmeow:expectedViolationCode pins the export\-binding code this fixture exists to demonstrate\.
- **Do:** `tests/conformance-fixtures/pvalue-tri-slice.ttl`
  - The signature round\-trip as one grounded chain: the sentence 'the p\-value was 0\.03' as a lang:SurfaceForm realizing an analyzed lang:ComposedForm, a lang:Denotation \(lang:denotesLogicFormula\) whose lang:denotationTarget is a logic:Formula, and that formula's first argument \(logic:termIri\) being the math:PValue\. The math:PValue carries its whole frame — a math:testStatistic, a math:nullHypothesis, a parameterized math:nullDistribution \(a math:SamplingDistribution\), and a math:alternativeSidedness that IS one of the six lawful math:Sidedness values \(math:twoSidedAlternative\) — with its magnitude a framed math:ProbabilityValue \(exact 3/100 in \[0, 1\]\)\. Every arm of math:IllFramedPValueShape is satisfied so its SPARQL stays silent, the lawful sidedness satisfies math:AlternativeSidednessValueShape's sh:in, the framed value satisfies math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape / math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape / math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape / math:RationalValueShape, and the null distribution satisfies the P6a/P6b/P7 gates, so validation emits no findings\.
- **Don't:** `tests/counter-examples/pvalue-tri-slice-illframed.ttl`
  - **Violation code:** `shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent`
  - The counter\-example is the SAME lang: \-\> logic: \-\> math: round\-trip fully grounded — a lang:SurfaceForm realizing a lang:ComposedForm, a lang:Denotation targeting a logic:Formula, and that formula predicating over the math:PValue — EXCEPT the p\-value omits BOTH math:tailDefinition AND math:alternativeSidedness, so the tail\-or\-sidedness arm of math:IllFramedPValueShape fires\. math:AlternativeSidednessValueShape's sh:in is satisfied vacuously \(no math:alternativeSidedness value to check\), the framed value still satisfies the probability\-value shapes, and the null distribution keeps the distribution gates silent, so validation MUST emit shacl\.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding \(math:IllFramedPValue\)\.
- **Do:** `tests/conformance-fixtures/review-projection-complete.ttl`
  - A gmeow:WorkReviewProjection over a continuing gmeow:WorkCluster carrying all eight contents — goal\-and\-recurrence, prescription lineage, current occurrence, derived frontier, approvals\-and\-pending, effect status, accumulated record, timeline — plus the gmeow:reviewReceipt that discloses what the projection collapsed, and a gmeow:FrontierExplanation whose gmeow:explanationProof names a real derivation\. gmeow:ReviewProjectionCompletenessConstraint and gmeow:ExplanationCarriesProofConstraint therefore both stay silent and validation emits no finding\. The contents are not eight blank nodes: each resolves into the cluster it summarises, so the frontier the review names is the frontier whose entries carry their hard failures, and the occurrence it names is the one that pinned its own input generation\.
- **Don't:** `tests/counter-examples/explanation-stands-on-narrative.ttl`
  - **Violation code:** `shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent`
  - The conforming scene with the gmeow:explanationProof binding removed and a model\-authored narrative standing in its place as ordinary evidence\. Everything a reader looks at first survives — the entry explained, the verifier verdict, the governing norm, the criterion with its dimensioned magnitude, the retained dissent — so the record has the SHAPE of a warrant while carrying nothing that can be recomputed\. That richness is the hazard: a bare narrative with no evidence and no policy is obviously an opinion, and this one is not\. MUST emit shacl\.SPARQLConstraintComponent from gmeow:ExplanationCarriesProofConstraintProceduralConstraintShape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI\. Its sibling gmeow:ReviewProjectionCompletenessConstraint stays silent: the review projection carries all eight contents and its receipt\.
- **Don't:** `tests/counter-examples/review-omits-its-preservation-receipt.ttl`
  - **Violation code:** `shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent`
  - The conforming scene with the gmeow:reviewReceipt binding removed\. The closure witness is still in the graph — the run computed it and enumerated every predicate it settled — and the review simply does not cite it, which is why an operator reading this surface cannot tell 'no dissent was recorded' from 'dissent was collapsed away'\. All eight contents remain, so the surface reads as complete to exactly the reader it misleads\. MUST emit shacl\.SPARQLConstraintComponent from gmeow:ReviewProjectionCompletenessConstraintProceduralConstraintShape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI\. Its sibling gmeow:ExplanationCarriesProofConstraint stays silent: the scene's frontier explanation carries its derivation\.
- See the [conformance fixtures index](../../fixtures/index.md).
